  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S Ashoka Biryani vs State Of Chhattisgarh on 14 June, 2024 Author: Parth Prateem Sahu Bench: Parth Prateem Sahu 1 Nafr High Court Of Chhattisgarh, Bilaspur Wpc No. 2629 of 2024 1- M/s Ashoka Biryani, Through Its Partner Kalpana Tiwari D/o Shri Ram Chandra Tiwari, Aged About 43 Years, R/o G-1420, Millennium Chowk, Sundar Nagar, Near Football House, P.S.- D.D. Nagar, Raipur, Distt. - Raipur, C.G. 2- Kalpana Tiwari, Partner- M/s Ashoka Biryani D/o Shri Ram Chandra Tiwari, Aged About 45 Years, R/o G-1420, Millennium Chowk, Sundar Nagar, Near Football House, P.S.- D.D. Nagar, Raipur, Distt. - Raipur, C.G. 3- Animesh Pandey, Partner -M/s Ashoka Biryani, S/o Shri Vibhuti Bhushan Pandey, Aged About 29 Years, R/o Agroha Colony, Near Raipura Chowk, P.S.- D.D. Nagar, Raipur, Distt. - Raipur, C.G. ---- Petitioners Versus 1- State Of Chhattisgarh, Through Collector, Raipur, Distt. - Raipur, C.G. 2- Municipal Corporation Raipur, Through Commissioner, Municipal Corporation Raipur, Distt. - Raipur, C.G. 3- Tahsildar, Tahsil And Distt. - Raipur, C.G. ---- Respondents For Petitioners : Mr. Kishore Bhaduri, Sr. Advocate with Mr. Ashutosh Pandey, Advocate & Mr. Sabyasachi Bhaduri, Advocate For Respondents/State : Mr. Keshav Prasad Gupta, G.A. For Respondent No.2 : Mr. Pankaj Agrawal, Advocate Hon'ble Shri Justice Parth Prateem Sahu Order On Board 14/06/2024Sd/- Sd/- 1. M/S Ashoka Biryani vs State Of Chhattisgarh on 14 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/44893583/ 1 2.",
    "facts": "From perusal of the panchnama or action, it is only appearing that shops were sealed under the order of Zone Commissioner, Municipal Corporation, Raipur who has no jurisdiction and authority of law to seal the business premises of petitioners for the lapses, if any, found as mentioned in the Panchanama. After inspection of business premises shortcomings and the irregularities were found. Municipal Corporation submits that the joint inspection was conducted and thereafter, three shops of petitioners were sealed under the order of Zone Commissioner, Zone - 9, Raipur and two shops have been sealed by State officials.",
    "arguments": "If any order or action is to be taken for lapses or irregularities, if any, found in the business premises of petitioners then it is the appropriate authority who could have taken action against petitioners. At this stage, learned counsel for petitioners submits that petitioners are under an obligation to comply with the permission/license which was issued by the competent authority permitting petitioners for running their business, however, the action on the part of the respondents is per-se M/S Ashoka Biryani vs State Of Chhattisgarh on 14 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/44893583/ 2 arbitrary, illegal and therefore, this petition be allowed. He relied upon the decision of this Court in case of E.S. Beena & Anr. Vs. State of Chhattisgarh, through : Principal Secretary & Ors., reported in 2022 SCC OnLine Chh. 1454. 8."
  },
